body:
If you ever want to work on the `window` of your application under test, you'll want to use [`cy.window()`](https://on.cypress.io/window), otherwise - you will be trying to access the actual Cypress Test Runner window.

Can you try:

```js
describe('page', () => {
    it('works', () => {
    });

    it('location.replace', () => {
		cy.window().then((win) => {
        	win.location.replace("");
		})
    })

    it('location.replace promise', () => {
		cy.window().then((win) => {
     		setTimeout(() =>{
          		win.location.replace("");
      		});
		})
    })
})
```

issue.body:
### Current behavior:

After visiting a site through `cy.visit` and accessing the window object with: 
`cy.window().then(win => {...})` we can not change the hash of the site with `win.location.replace('#bar')`. Using `win.location.hash = '#bar'` instead works flawlessly. 

Calling `win.location.replace` redirects the iFrame of the tested page to a URL with a `__` prefix, the `__` could come from the main document window? (where the cypress runner lives). 

1. the runner loads `index.html`
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6185006/66873905-7dea9280-ef5e-11e9-93b5-309bdcca653b.png)
2. calling `win.location.replace("#bar");` within `cy.window().then(win => {...})` should lead to URL `http://localhost:52402/index.html#bar`, but instead leads to:
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6185006/66873985-b5593f00-ef5e-11e9-86ef-2051525dc8d5.png)

This is an issue for us, because we currently try to test a website, which heavily uses `win.location.replace` and if the cypress runner opens this site in the iFrame the window-object of the website somehow gets altered through cypress and the `win.location.replace` leads to the redirection error described above. **The error occurs irrespective of whether we call the redirect function from the `cy.window()`-callback or directly from within the website context.** Any idea why this is happening?

### Desired behavior:
`window.location.replace` should just change the hash and not crash the page

### Steps to reproduce: 
I created a small repo where the error is reproduced in a minimal setup. 

https://github.com/davidhennemann/cypressBugDemo

Basically just open any website and afterwards execute:
```js
it("should work", () => {
  cy.visit("https://cypress.io");

  cy.wait(2000);
  cy.window().then(win => {
    // this works
    win.location.hash = "#foo";
    // this will lead to a cypress crash
    win.location.replace("#bar");
  });
});
```

